233
00:23:10,052 --> 00:23:13,312
We also have information about the entities that are acquiring or applying the

234
00:23:13,352 --> 00:23:15,832
restrictions that was not shared via a standard.

235
00:23:15,992 --> 00:23:17,492
We have information on

236
00:23:19,152 --> 00:23:23,012
where and how unrestricted data can be accessed, and we have

237
00:23:23,052 --> 00:23:24,952
more detailed information on what has been withheld.

238
00:23:25,192 --> 00:23:26,572
So these are the sort of things we'd like,

239
00:23:27,812 --> 00:23:31,712
hopefully in the future, to be able to share via our Darwin Core Archives or

240
00:23:31,752 --> 00:23:32,992
Darwin Core data packages.

241
00:23:34,212 --> 00:23:37,412
And hopefully, I think we'll hear some more about the work that the task group has

242
00:23:37,472 --> 00:23:37,672
been

243
00:23:39,252 --> 00:23:42,912
working on to expand the Darwin Core standard such that this sort of

244
00:23:42,952 --> 00:23:44,692
information might be available in the future.

245
00:23:45,392 --> 00:23:46,032
But I think that's

