1221
01:21:20,650 --> 01:21:24,250
So as you've-- This is probably just rehashing what everybody else has said, but

1222
01:21:24,310 --> 01:21:28,210
sensitive species data are basically data about species that have features

1223
01:21:28,250 --> 01:21:32,150
that mean there are reasons for withholding the data from public view or modifying

1224
01:21:32,190 --> 01:21:33,970
the data before it is made public.

1225
01:21:34,850 --> 01:21:38,430
And we're tending to use the terminology of restricted access

1226
01:21:38,450 --> 01:21:41,990
species data within the task group now because of the word

1227
01:21:42,010 --> 01:21:45,830
"sensitive" tends to cause people to feel reticent about sharing their data

1228
01:21:45,890 --> 01:21:48,970
rather than about making it open, but in a way that protects

1229
01:21:49,770 --> 01:21:51,310
the sensitivities of the data.

1230
01:21:53,030 --> 01:21:56,390
And most of what the task group has been talking about is how we can go about

1231
01:21:56,430 --> 01:21:58,910
protecting the importance of this kind of sensitive data,

1232
01:21:59,950 --> 01:22:03,870
but still allow the data to be accessible in some form to

1233
01:22:03,930 --> 01:22:05,010
people who need to see it.

1234
01:22:05,850 --> 01:22:09,110
That includes people like researchers or decision-makers.

1235
01:22:10,110 --> 01:22:10,410
So

1236
01:22:11,730 --> 01:22:12,830
the image on this page,

1237
01:22:14,590 --> 01:22:18,170
as you've seen similar examples from other

1238
01:22:18,250 --> 01:22:22,070
speakers today, it provides a practical example of

1239
01:22:22,130 --> 01:22:22,290
what

1240
01:22:23,570 --> 01:22:26,130
this looks like in practice. So on

1241
01:22:27,650 --> 01:22:28,910
the bottom left-hand side

1242
01:22:30,430 --> 01:22:31,910
are records for a species that is

1243
01:22:31,970 --> 01:22:36,270
sensitive

1244
01:22:36,990 --> 01:22:40,290
in South Australia, which is on the right-hand side, and the left-hand side is not

1245
01:22:40,890 --> 01:22:44,130
considered sensitive, which is in the state of Victoria in Australia.

1246
01:22:46,110 --> 01:22:48,590
So you can see we basically do a similar

1247
01:22:49,890 --> 01:22:53,650
treatment to others where we generalize the data or

1248
01:22:53,710 --> 01:22:53,890
we

1249
01:22:54,790 --> 01:22:55,730
basically snap it to

1250
01:22:57,670 --> 01:22:59,210
either a one- or 10-degree grid.

1251
01:23:01,230 --> 01:23:05,110
So another feature of restricted access species data that it tends to

1252
01:23:05,310 --> 01:23:09,230
vary on the data custodian that we're talking to or

1253
01:23:09,270 --> 01:23:10,870
the administration that you're dealing with.

1254
01:23:11,250 --> 01:23:11,510
So

1255
01:23:13,750 --> 01:23:15,450
as you can see there as an example.

1256
01:23:16,950 --> 01:23:19,830
So the RASD reasons that we've come up with

1257
01:23:21,070 --> 01:23:22,610
to form the vocabulary.

1258
01:23:24,790 --> 01:23:27,390
So they're things like personal information and privacy,

1259
01:23:29,970 --> 01:23:32,890
which may either be a lack of consent or

1260
01:23:33,530 --> 01:23:37,270
someone's asked for request for privacy for their information.

1261
01:23:39,330 --> 01:23:43,270
Sensitive species location, so this might be where a

1262
01:23:44,530 --> 01:23:47,550
species is highly restricted, there's a threatened

1263
01:23:47,610 --> 01:23:51,510
population, there's exposure via survey

1264
01:23:51,610 --> 01:23:52,530
information.

1265
01:23:54,210 --> 01:23:54,870
Don't know why it went--

1266
01:24:00,530 --> 01:24:04,310
Or a potential harm to people or property, or there might be

1267
01:24:04,710 --> 01:24:06,670
a lack of information about the species.

1268
01:24:08,230 --> 01:24:11,870
Biosecurity risk, so there might be trade species or invasive

1269
01:24:11,950 --> 01:24:12,650
species.

1270
01:24:14,510 --> 01:24:15,850
Species attributes might

1271
01:24:17,930 --> 01:24:19,970
be something that might need to be restricted.

1272
01:24:20,050 --> 01:24:21,850
So other people have talked about

1273
01:24:22,970 --> 01:24:25,750
things like roosting sites or nesting

1274
01:24:28,630 --> 01:24:32,510
occurrences. So that sort of information might be something that might be

1275
01:24:32,550 --> 01:24:36,030
restricted within a record, not the whole record itself.

1276
01:24:37,730 --> 01:24:40,110
And there may be usage restrictions on the data.

1277
01:24:40,150 --> 01:24:43,750
So there might be a legal contract or other reasons

1278
01:24:44,130 --> 01:24:45,750
for withholding the data or

1279
01:24:47,410 --> 01:24:48,910
