predate handheld GPS.

3174
03:31:12,630 --> 03:31:16,450
The other thing that we like about sharing the data through GBIF is that we know

3175
03:31:16,510 --> 03:31:19,890
how people use it. So we've got all these citations of the data where

3176
03:31:20,670 --> 03:31:24,090
did it from GBIF and used it in their place.

3177
03:31:25,670 --> 03:31:29,530
We took apart the

3178
03:31:30,130 --> 03:31:33,690
metadata about how downloads were generated through GBIF.

3179
03:31:34,090 --> 03:31:37,950
So for all of those citations, then I pulled down the

3180
03:31:37,990 --> 03:31:41,590
way that those downloads have been delimited and looked at the predicates that

3181
03:31:41,630 --> 03:31:43,490
people use to form the queries

3182
03:31:44,310 --> 03:31:47,490
to get that data, and two-thirds of them use spatial predicates.

3183
03:31:48,170 --> 03:31:50,370
So two-thirds of them throw away most of our data.

3184
03:31:52,130 --> 03:31:54,350
So yeah, we think that's a real problem.

3185
03:31:55,110 --> 03:31:57,630
That two-thirds figure, that's just done on

3186
03:31:59,210 --> 03:32:01,130
Kew data that's shared through GBIF.

3187
03:32:01,870 --> 03:32:05,090
But if you're sat in the audience and you want to make the same argument

3188
03:32:05,150 --> 03:32:09,030
to your managers or your curators, all that data is available

3189
03:32:09,090 --> 03:32:12,870
to do the same kind of analysis for any other dataset that's shared through

3190
03:32:12,930 --> 03:32:14,210
GBIF. So you can see how

3191
03:32:15,090 --> 03:32:16,450
people are querying it and

3192
03:32:17,630 --> 03:32:21,450
what bits of the specimen record you should prioritize for

3193
03:32:21,850 --> 03:32:22,330
management.

3194
03:32:23,490 --> 03:32:24,590
So we know that we need to

3195
03:32:25,430 --> 03:32:29,250
turn those descriptions of places into things that are computable because that's

3196
03:32:29,290 --> 03:32:30,930
the way that people want to get at our data.

3197
03:32:34,650 --> 03:32:36,850
And we've got some data that will help us get at that.

3198
03:32:37,550 --> 03:32:37,830
So

3199
03:32:38,910 --> 03:32:42,890
this is our specimen sheet, and I'd argue that it's

3200
