nicer than a pinned insect because there's loads of data on it.

3201
03:32:46,430 --> 03:32:46,610
But

3202
03:32:48,050 --> 03:32:51,670
there are a couple of pieces of data on it that help us disambiguate

3203
03:32:52,350 --> 03:32:55,550
from where this specimen was collected, even though we only have a description of

3204
03:32:55,570 --> 03:32:56,010
the place.

3205
03:32:58,050 --> 03:32:59,970
So yes. We have

3206
03:33:01,590 --> 03:33:01,990
a date,

3207
03:33:03,050 --> 03:33:06,850
and we have a number that the collector puts on their collecting events as

3208
03:33:06,910 --> 03:33:07,110
they

3209
03:33:08,230 --> 03:33:08,670
collect them.

3210
03:33:10,330 --> 03:33:10,550
And

3211
03:33:11,570 --> 03:33:13,950
collectors are great people, and some of my best friends are

3212
03:33:15,070 --> 03:33:18,210
botanical collectors, but they are bound by the laws of the universe.

3213
03:33:18,270 --> 03:33:20,430
They can only move forward through time, right?

3214
03:33:20,870 --> 03:33:22,690
And they can only move through space.

3215
03:33:23,530 --> 03:33:24,290
And as they do that,

3216
03:33:26,250 --> 03:33:28,630
they're putting numbers on the things that they pick up,

3217
03:33:29,550 --> 03:33:33,270
and they're ascending, right? You've got time on the bottom and number on the--

3218
03:33:33,650 --> 03:33:34,990
time on the bottom axis,

3219
03:33:36,890 --> 03:33:37,770
record number on the

3220
03:33:38,690 --> 03:33:41,250
y-axis, and they're ticking up through time as they do that.

3221
03:33:41,810 --> 03:33:45,750
So we should be able to use an algorithm to crawl along that trace and find all

3222
03:33:45,790 --> 03:33:49,670
those records that fit together from one person's work.

3223
03:33:50,750 --> 03:33:51,610
And someone else's work

3224
03:33:52,530 --> 03:33:56,310
might be within the same timeframe, but because they're allocating a different

3225
03:33:57,090 --> 03:33:59,510
set of numbers, we should be able to disambiguate them.

3226
03:34:01,350 --> 03:34:05,050
And with that, those adjacent collecting events should be spatially

3227
03:34:05,110 --> 03:34:08,130
adjacent, right? They're not hopping between different continents.

3228
03:34:08,770 --> 03:34:11,710
They should be close together, so they're easier to georeference because we know

3229
03:34:11,750 --> 03:34:12,550
that they're close by.

