3849
05:39:23,966 --> 05:39:27,126
CSV files in a frictionless data package.

3850
05:39:28,426 --> 05:39:32,186
Technical staff at an organization can write scripts against these,

3851
05:39:32,346 --> 05:39:36,326
and non-technical staff likewise can browse through them and

3852
05:39:36,406 --> 05:39:37,986
open them up in a spreadsheet editor.

3853
05:39:39,346 --> 05:39:43,206
A unique list of users, records that might be missing attributions

3854
05:39:43,366 --> 05:39:46,966
altogether, some whose collecting dates are in logical

3855
05:39:47,026 --> 05:39:50,766
conflict with collector birth or death dates, and other similar kinds of

3856
05:39:50,846 --> 05:39:54,686
files are all itemized in a descriptor, and then everything is

3857
05:39:54,726 --> 05:39:57,546
pushed into Zenodo so that you can retrieve at any time you wish.

3858
05:39:58,866 --> 05:40:02,366
A Bionomia HTML badge can also be pasted into an

3859
05:40:02,426 --> 05:40:06,246
organization's own webpage to help engender a bit more visibility in this process.

3860
05:40:08,966 --> 05:40:12,346
After many years of helping organizations integrate some of these

3861
05:40:12,546 --> 05:40:16,366
CSV files into their workflows while also reprocessing

3862
05:40:16,866 --> 05:40:20,746
new data from GBIF into Bionomia on a monthly basis, I've tried to

3863
05:40:20,786 --> 05:40:23,526
document numerous persistent challenges.

3864
05:40:24,646 --> 05:40:28,165
Round-tripping is nowhere near as easy as we might have assumed.

3865
05:40:28,686 --> 05:40:32,606
A view no doubt shared by the Filtered Push project that aspired to

3866
05:40:32,666 --> 05:40:36,626
