4025
05:48:12,278 --> 05:48:16,238
undertaken by the wider biodiversity community because we believe that Wikidata

4026
05:48:16,278 --> 05:48:20,078
can actually play a pivotal role in interlinking the data and sources for

4027
05:48:20,138 --> 05:48:21,018
type specimens.

4028
05:48:24,098 --> 05:48:27,638
Another motivator for this work is the potential for natural history institutions

4029
05:48:27,698 --> 05:48:31,658
to add to, add or at least link to these Wikidata items in their

4030
05:48:31,698 --> 05:48:35,418
collection management systems, and also in other natural history

4031
05:48:35,478 --> 05:48:39,457
databases. And this reuse would make it easier for anyone to trace

4032
05:48:39,637 --> 05:48:43,618
where these important physical specimens are held and would also improve the

4033
05:48:43,678 --> 05:48:47,518
findability of data about those specimens, including the publications

4034
