crosswalking mappings between the model and Darwin Core.

4100
05:53:01,986 --> 05:53:05,686
We also uploaded our documentation into Wikimedia Commons, so you can easily

4101
05:53:05,726 --> 05:53:06,426
download it there.

4102
05:53:07,406 --> 05:53:11,266
To make the documentation accessible to a wider audience, we added it

4103
05:53:11,326 --> 05:53:15,086
to the research repository Zenodo, and importantly, we formed a

4104
05:53:15,146 --> 05:53:16,046
Zenodo community.

4105
05:53:16,846 --> 05:53:20,406
We created this for this project, and it includes an Excel spreadsheet

4106
05:53:20,466 --> 05:53:23,306
generated from the OpenRefine upload that I discussed earlier.

4107
05:53:24,186 --> 05:53:28,166
All of this was aimed at helping guide institutions and editors

4108
05:53:28,226 --> 05:53:31,786
when creating or enriching type specimen items in Wikidata.

4109
05:53:35,086 --> 05:53:38,666
We've curated exemplar holotype Wikidata items, and these

4110
05:53:38,766 --> 05:53:42,666
items illustrate the data model and show just some of the sources of data

4111
05:53:42,706 --> 05:53:45,646
and identifiers that can be linked via Wikidata.

4112
05:53:46,066 --> 05:53:49,566
So for example, there is an exemplar Wikidata item for a

4113
05:53:49,626 --> 05:53:53,486
holotype that was first observed in iNaturalist, as well as an item

4114
05:53:53,526 --> 05:53:57,246
that links to the Disco generated DOI for the digital record of that

4115
05:53:57,326 --> 05:53:57,786
specimen.

4116
05:54:01,986 --> 05:54:05,186
And here's a list of the Wikidata properties currently being used in the model.

4117
05:54:05,586 --> 05:54:09,126
Now, these properties obviously help enrich the type specimen item with

4118
05:54:09,166 --> 05:54:11,226
semantically linked data statements.

4119
05:54:15,726 --> 05:54:19,026
And importantly, identifiers have also been added to items

4120
05:54:19,646 --> 05:54:23,426
if Wikidata properties exist for those identifiers.

