05:54:23,846 --> 05:54:27,806
So in this slide, you can see an example of where an iNaturalist observation ID

4122
05:54:27,866 --> 05:54:30,546
for that type specimen has been added to the item.

4123
05:54:30,946 --> 05:54:34,886
And if a Wikidata property for an identifier does not actually currently exist,

4124
05:54:35,206 --> 05:54:38,926
the data can still be linked via the describedat URL property.

4125
05:54:43,726 --> 05:54:47,126
Now, we recognize this data model is a work in progress, and

4126
05:54:47,186 --> 05:54:51,045
improvements can be made. For example, we've proposed

4127
05:54:51,105 --> 05:54:54,906
the creation of a Wikidata property for the GBIF occurrence

4128
05:54:54,986 --> 05:54:58,746
ID. This is under discussion with the Wikidata community at the moment.

4129
05:54:59,766 --> 05:55:03,406
Currently, the basis of record data is modeled as an instance

4130
05:55:03,526 --> 05:55:04,426
of statement.

4131
05:55:05,466 --> 05:55:09,386
Ideally, a new Wikidata property should be proposed to describe the

4132
05:55:09,446 --> 05:55:12,746
nature of the record, improving alignment with Darwin Core.

4133
05:55:13,226 --> 05:55:17,206
Another area of future work is the incorporation of the preservation method of

4134
05:55:17,246 --> 05:55:21,146
the specimen. Again, to include this, a Wikidata property

4135
05:55:21,166 --> 05:55:24,466
proposal for the preservation method would also be required.

4136
05:55:25,266 --> 05:55:29,166
And last, but certainly not least, we also considered proposing a

4137
05:55:29,226 --> 05:55:33,186
Wikidata property for bicultural notices to support the inclusion

4138
05:55:33,286 --> 05:55:35,446
of local context notices in this model.

4139
05:55:36,346 --> 05:55:39,866
GBIF is pilot testing the traditional knowledge and bicultural

4140
05:55:39,926 --> 05:55:42,966
labels on occurrence records at the moment.

4141
05:55:43,526 --> 05:55:46,946
We very much support this work, but we decided to

4142
05:55:46,986 --> 05:55:50,886
delay any Wikidata property proposal until the infrastructure

4143
05:55:50,926 --> 05:55:54,386
and associated guidance exists in GBIF and in Darwin Core.

4144
05:55:58,246 --> 05:56:01,706
Now, I'm coming to the end of my presentation, but before I finish, I just want to

4145
05:56:01,786 --> 05:56:05,466
emphasize that one of the main benefits of Wikidata is that it

4146
05:56:05,506 --> 05:56:09,306
empowers anyone to create and enrich these types of items.

4147
05:56:10,006 --> 05:56:13,946
While creating holotype specimen items in line with our proposed model, I and

4148
05:56:14,026 --> 05:56:17,726
other Wiki editors like me have been able to digitally connect

4149
05:56:17,786 --> 05:56:21,666
collectors, determiners, localities, publications, collection dates,

4150
05:56:21,746 --> 05:56:24,066
significant events such as research expeditions,

4151
05:56:24,946 --> 05:56:28,306
and importantly, also ensure that the relevant identifiers are all

4152
05:56:28,366 --> 05:56:30,886
semantically linked to these in Wikidata.

4153
05:56:31,836 --> 05:56:35,456
Wikidata helps democratize this type of data curation

4154
05:56:35,936 --> 05:56:39,796
and empowers the wider biodiversity community to enrich and link data

4155
05:56:40,176 --> 05:56:43,816
related to these important specimens and ensuring everyone can

4156
05:56:43,856 --> 05:56:47,356
contribute to improving the visibility of these

4157
05:56:47,436 --> 05:56:51,376
specimens and the interoperability of their related

