4365
06:09:05,338 --> 06:09:08,358
specimens and other collection objects, participants,

4366
06:09:08,518 --> 06:09:11,878
institutions, localities, itineraries,

4367
06:09:12,218 --> 06:09:14,118
publications, and archival records.

4368
06:09:14,638 --> 06:09:18,618
In other words, identify the expedition, describe it once, and

4369
06:09:18,658 --> 06:09:22,338
then link to the distributed evidence and objects,

4370
06:09:23,118 --> 06:09:24,118
link them back to it.

4371
06:09:26,058 --> 06:09:29,778
Particular emphasis is placed on interoperability with Darwin Core

4372
06:09:30,298 --> 06:09:33,858
and the use of persistent Wikidata identifiers, and also the

4373
06:09:33,918 --> 06:09:37,398
collaborative community curation of expedition

4374
06:09:37,438 --> 06:09:40,178
metadata, which is done within Wikidata.

4375
06:09:40,658 --> 06:09:44,638
And as a complement to, or an alternative to maintaining

4376
06:09:45,238 --> 06:09:49,078
all the expedition metadata exclusively within the collection management

4377
06:09:49,158 --> 06:09:49,578
system,

4378
06:09:50,778 --> 06:09:54,718
they can be placed in Wikidata and then the identifiers integrated in the

4379
06:09:54,758 --> 06:09:58,218
collection management systems. So our recommendations

4380
06:09:58,698 --> 06:10:02,618
or some first recommendations are to create new or enrich

4381
