The idea is to bring together natural history collections

5772
07:49:36,056 --> 07:49:39,756
data from across institutions to have a single platform for

5773
07:49:39,796 --> 07:49:41,136
community curation.

5774
07:49:42,776 --> 07:49:45,876
So digitizing the collections, it's important.

5775
07:49:46,656 --> 07:49:49,856
Again, five minutes, so I'm going to assume everyone's on the same page here.

5776
07:49:50,916 --> 07:49:54,376
And we have been making very good progress as a community

5777
07:49:54,436 --> 07:49:58,396
digitizing the collections. However, it is getting difficult to scale

5778
07:49:58,496 --> 07:50:02,056
up. Sometimes the lower hanging fruit has been immediately

5779
07:50:02,116 --> 07:50:06,076
targeted, and now we're stuck with stuff that is a little harder to

5780
07:50:06,136 --> 07:50:06,796
digitize.

5781
07:50:07,896 --> 07:50:10,876
Institutions are working independently from one another.

5782
07:50:10,956 --> 07:50:14,896
There's less opportunity for collaboration, and there's a lot

5783
07:50:14,996 --> 07:50:18,776
of manual tasks that are just begging to be automated.

5784
07:50:19,576 --> 07:50:20,236
So what we get

5785
07:50:21,376 --> 07:50:24,876
is a system where different institutions are developing

5786
07:50:25,396 --> 07:50:29,376
more or less the same thing. And sometimes that's a question of people not

5787
07:50:29,416 --> 07:50:33,216
being aware of what the other institutions are doing, and sometimes it's a question

5788
07:50:33,316 --> 07:50:37,276
of everyone's data is so radically different from one another

5789
07:50:37,356 --> 07:50:40,916
that to bring one system, one digital

5790
07:50:40,976 --> 07:50:44,916
service to another institution would require so much time

5791
07:50:44,956 --> 07:50:45,536
to rework.

5792
07:50:46,516 --> 07:50:48,216
And so that's sort of where Disco comes in.

5793
07:50:48,956 --> 07:50:52,156
So Disco, this research infrastructure,

5794
07:50:55,076 --> 07:50:58,936
we've brought a bunch of data from different institutions

5795
07:50:59,016 --> 07:51:01,136
under the same structure. And so

5796
07:51:02,496 --> 07:51:06,336
digital services that aid and augment the data, if they are

5797
07:51:06,415 --> 07:51:09,416
adapted to Disco, can all of a sudden be brought into any

5798
07:51:09,476 --> 07:51:11,736
institution that is a partner of Disco.

5799
07:51:12,696 --> 07:51:15,436
We call these services machine annotation services.

5800
07:51:17,816 --> 07:51:21,116
And these are a few of our pilot machine annotation

5801
07:51:21,176 --> 07:51:24,436
