5803
07:51:27,856 --> 07:51:27,996
So,

5804
07:51:29,236 --> 07:51:32,476
we have a plant organ detection service using Leaf Machine.

5805
07:51:32,636 --> 07:51:35,996
We can link to other infrastructures, GBIF, ENA,

5806
07:51:36,796 --> 07:51:40,316
Geocase. We use GeoPic, which is developed by GBIF,

5807
07:51:41,596 --> 07:51:45,436
to georeference specimens. And most excitingly, we have a

5808
07:51:45,476 --> 07:51:49,376
label transcription tool, so we use Votervision to read labels

5809
07:51:49,416 --> 07:51:51,696
and then transcribe that into Darwin Core.

5810
07:51:52,956 --> 07:51:56,856
And what you'll notice, all of these things in bold, we don't develop them.

5811
07:51:56,976 --> 07:51:59,436
We've just adapted them to the infrastructure.

5812
07:51:59,996 --> 07:52:03,336
And now, we've talked a little bit about these services in Disco

5813
07:52:03,956 --> 07:52:07,336
for a couple of TadWigs now. But what's exciting is that we

5814
07:52:07,416 --> 07:52:10,976
